    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-12613",
      "problem": "What is the value of $\\cos 225^\\circ?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's remind ourselves of the special trigonometric ratios, as given by the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14250054/assets/d93c490adbb5cdbc0e9a09b60eea9b82ab93be8e871e334423abc17ddd62955e.png)\n\nFrom the unit circle, we see that the angle $225^\\circ$ corresponds to the point $\\left( -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}, -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\right).$\n\nSince the cosine of the angle corresponds to the $x$-coordinate, we have $\\cos 225^\\circ  = -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.$",
